%I A402431 #13 Nov 21 2026 23:09:15
%S A402431 3,5,7,17,29,43,53,79,277,521,1087,2399,2543,4831,5657,22109,88903,
%T A402431 92831
%N A402431 Primes p > 2 such that either (4/3)*p# + 1 or (8/3)*p# + 1 is prime, where prime(n)# = A002110(n).
%C A402431 Primes prime(n) such that A402500(n) is prime.
%C A402431 One of (4/3)*p# + 1 and (8/3)*p# + 1 is divisible by 3 and the other one is congruent to 2 modulo 3.
%C A402431 a(19) > 10^5. - _Michael S. Branicky_, Nov 21 2026
%e A402431 2*8+1 = 17 is prime, so 3 is a term;
%e A402431 8*5+1 = 41 is prime, so 5 is a term;
%e A402431 8*5*7+1 = 281 is prime, so 7 is a term;
%e A402431 2*8*5*7*11+1 = 6161 = 61*101, so 11 is not a term;
%e A402431 2*8*5*7*11*13+1 = 80081 = 73*1097, so 13 is not a term;
%e A402431 8*5*7*11*13*17+1 = 680681 is prime, so 17 is a term;
%e A402431 8*5*7*11*13*17*19+1 = 12932921 = 31*417191, so 19 is not a term.
%o A402431 (PARI) my(P=8); forprime(p=5, 1000, P*=p; if(ispseudoprime(P+1) || ispseudoprime(2*P+1), print1(p, ", ")))
%Y A402431 Cf. A002110 (primorials), A102476 (4 times primorials), A402500.
%Y A402431 See A402499 for a list of related sequences.
%K A402431 nonn,more,new
%O A402431 1,1
%A A402431 _Jianing Song_, Nov 18 2026
%E A402431 a(17)-a(18) from _Michael S. Branicky_, Nov 21 2026
